    "id": "56c5d8ed0e4f9f3be3d42f01ad6b7b6fb62ba04e",
    "tree_id": "d1f8db2cee81d9e0a6ea13883707aa448afbca77",
    "message": "Fix the Android build: the Gradle configuration cache, not Kotlin, not ARM\n\nEvery multi-ABI Gecko/AAR pass died at :geckoview:compileDebugKotlin with\n\n  Could not LOAD the value of field `__buildFusService__` ... Cannot set the\n  value of a property of type BuildFusService using a provider of type\n  FlowActionBuildFusService\n\nThe operative word is LOAD. This is configuration-cache deserialization, not\nservice registration: the Kotlin Gradle plugin writes its FUS usage-statistics\nbuild service into the cache as FlowActionBuildFusService and reads it back\ninto a field declared BuildFusService. The types do not round-trip, so the\ncache is not stale but unusable - deleting it does not help, and a freshly\nwritten entry fails identically.\n\nTwo things disguised this, and both are recorded in the patch header because\nthe next intermittent Kotlin failure will look the same:\n\n  * The configuration cache lives in the SOURCE tree at\n    <srcdir>/.gradle/configuration-cache, not in --outdir. Every \"clean fresh\n    outdir\" run silently reused it.\n  * armeabi-v7a is both first in DEFAULT_ABIS and the default --fat-host-abi,\n    so a 3-ABI run always failed on it and the other two ABIs never ran. That\n    produced an \"ARM-specific\" conclusion from a single data point. Re-testing\n    x86_64 on 2026-08-24 failed identically; the ABI was never the variable.\n\nThree diagnoses were drawn and acted on before this one. None held: ARM\nspecificity; a stale cache; and a Kotlin 2.3.21-vs-2.3.20 version mismatch.\nThat last one is real - Gradle 9.5.1 embeds kotlin-dsl 2.3.20 and the build log\nflags the mismatch itself - but it is harmless, and aligning it changed\nnothing. patches/android/kotlin-version-alignment.patch is therefore DROPPED\nrather than kept: it fixed no observed fault and was an unproven divergence\nfrom upstream that every future rebase would have to carry. Its two\nREVIEWED_ORDER_FREE pairs are removed from check-patch-order.py with it.\n\nMeasured 2026-08-24: with the cache off, :geckoview:compileDebugKotlin\ncompletes at upstream's Kotlin 2.3.21 and the build proceeds into the Rust\nstage. The cost is negligible - the configuration cache accelerates the\nCONFIGURATION phase of repeated builds, and these are from-scratch container\nrelease builds where configuration is a rounding error against a ~20 minute\ncompile.\n\nLanded as a patch, not a tree edit: gradle.properties lives in the extracted\nFirefox tree, so an edit there is wiped by the next `make dir` and is invisible\nto every gate. That is landmine L4.\n\nAll six cheap gates green: 81 patch files (24 common, 36 desktop, 21 android),\n11/11 ordering constraints, 60 shared-file pairs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
